{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>At the appointed time of which He spoke.</b> Rashi's explanation: when He said to him 'at the appointed time I will return to you,' He made a scratch for him in the wall. And if you ask: but we said above that He was standing in Tishrei, as we said 'at the appointed time I will return to you,' and it is established for us that Isaac was born on Pesach! One may answer that in Nisan and in Tishrei the nights and days are equal, and the sun shines through the same window in both."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:08.389032001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}